Member creation: username, password policy, and no secret in the audit log

Three defects in createPerson, all found by reading it against the
previous system's equivalent:

- The plaintext password was spread into the audit trail. It is now
  omitted and only `hasPassword` is recorded. Audit rows are widely
  readable and nobody expects a secret in one.
- No password policy at creation, while changing a password enforced one.
  A password rejected by the change form could be planted at creation.
- Email uniqueness compared case-sensitively while the database index is
  case-insensitive, so "A@x.com" passed the guard and then hit a raw
  Postgres error instead of a readable message.

Also adds an optional username at creation, matching the login form which
already accepted either identifier, validated by the same rule the setup
wizard uses.

